# Build-context hygiene, and it is a memory/disk issue before it is a
# tidiness one.
#
# Docker sends the whole build context to the daemon BEFORE any COPY runs, so
# this list applies even though no Dockerfile in this repo COPYs from the
# context today (verified against docker/Dockerfile.flink, .connect and .dbt,
# all of which install from the network and mount at runtime instead).
#
# The project lives on an NTFS mount (/mnt/F). .venv alone is tens of
# thousands of files, and dbt/target is regenerated on every `make dbt`, so
# without this every `make flink-up` and `make connect-up` pays to transfer
# and hash both of them for nothing.
#
# .env is here for a second reason: it holds the passwords, and there is no
# build that needs them. Compose substitutes them at runtime.
#
# PATTERNS ARE ANCHORED AT THE CONTEXT ROOT, and a bare name does not match at
# depth (unlike .gitignore). That is why `dbt/target` and `airflow/logs` are
# spelled out below rather than written as `target` and `logs`. Measured the hard
# way: `make pipeline-image` failed with
#
#     Can't add file .../airflow/logs/scheduler/2026-09-24/transit_health.py.log
#     to tar: archive/tar: write too long
#
# because Airflow appends to those files every few seconds and the tar raced one
# growing mid-build. The scheduler had only just been unpaused, which is what
# turned a latent problem into a visible one.

.git
.venv
.env
data
# Historical run logs from Phases 1-3 (1.7 MB), at the context root so the bare
# name matches. No build reads them.
logs
airflow/logs
dbt/target
dbt/logs
dbt/dbt_packages
dbt/.user.yml

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
